AI-powered company identity resolver for short/informal queries

Fixes the "typed 'inpost' → 0 articles / 25 irrelevant hits" class of bugs
by letting Claude normalise short inputs into the canonical Polish company
before the article scan runs.

- app/analysis/claude_analyzer.py: new `resolve_company_identity(query)`
  returns the legal name, sector, media aliases and (when confident)
  NIP/KRS for inputs like "inpost", "cd projekt", "pko", "zondacrypto".
- app/api/routes.py `quick_lookup` now:
    • calls the resolver for free-text queries, then looks the suggested
      NIP/KRS up in MF/KRS to get authoritative data,
    • validates the AI-supplied identifier against the registry name with
      rapidfuzz token-set similarity — rejects obvious hallucinations
      (e.g. Claude mapping "eurocash" to a NIP that actually belongs to
      Getin Noble Bank),
    • persists the canonical legal name and a rich alias set so that the
      scraper (NewsAPI / RSS / GDELT) uses every variant the press
      actually uses, not just the literal string the user typed,
    • returns `resolved_name / resolved_from / resolved_aliases` so the
      UI can tell the user how the input was interpreted.
- Frontend surfaces this: lookup status shows "AI rozpoznało: <canonical>
  (na podstawie '<input>'). Krok 2/2 · szukam artykułów…" with a toast.
- Articles panel: when every analysed article is `mentions_company=false`
  the page now shows a warning card explaining the likely cause (too
  generic a name) and offers one-click "Uruchom skan ponownie".
- Cache-bust static assets to v=3.
